    "## 4. Weak picks + leakage check\n",
    "\n",
    "The weakest part of this rule is its hard threshold. A page with 299 impressions receives no score while a page with 300 qualifies. That boundary is operationally convenient, not a natural law.\n",
    "\n",
    "Another weakness is that `days_since_last_update` is only as good as the update metadata. A genuinely refreshed page can still look stale if the source field was not updated.\n",
    "\n",
    "The rule also deliberately ignores position and CTR. That makes it simple, but it can miss pages that are already well positioned and have a clear CTR problem.\n"
   ]
  },
